{
  "id": "reverse_linked_list_ii",
  "title": "Reverse Linked List II",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Linked List"
  ],
  "description": "<p>Given the <code>head</code> of a singly linked list and two integers <code>left</code> and <code>right</code> where <code>left &lt;= right</code>, reverse the nodes of the list from position <code>left</code> to position <code>right</code>, and return <em>the reversed list</em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets/problem_images/96710cf1fd7e41aaaeee4d1a62ebb97a9eae7194571b55768a84a0ad26c3e418.jpg\" style=\"width: 542px; height: 222px;\" />\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> head = [1,2,3,4,5], left = 2, right = 4\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,4,3,2,5]\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> head = [5], left = 1, right = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> [5]\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The number of nodes in the list is <code>n</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 500</code></li>\n\t<li><code>-500 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 500</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= left &lt;= right &lt;= n</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<strong>Follow up:</strong> Could you do it in one pass?",
  "task": "Solve the 'Reverse Linked List II' problem on LeetCode.",
  "inputFormat": "Passed directly as parameters.",
  "outputFormat": "Returned value from the solution method.",
  "constraints": [
    "The number of nodes in the list is n.",
    "1 <= n <= 500",
    "-500 <= Node.val <= 500",
    "1 <= left <= right <= n"
  ],
  "hints": [],
  "method": {
    "name": "reverseBetween",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "head",
        "type": "list_node"
      },
      {
        "name": "left",
        "type": "int"
      },
      {
        "name": "right",
        "type": "int"
      }
    ]
  },
  "manifest": {
    "entry": {
